+Whether to enable IEEE-relaxed floating-point optimizations (FMA fusion, no NaN / infinity / signed-zero guarantees). Default `True`. On CUDA it also selects the approximate single-precision libdevice routines for `qd.sin`, `qd.cos`, `qd.log` and `qd.exp` (`__nv_fast_sinf` and friends, accurate to a few ulp over their intended input ranges; `f64` is never affected). Disable when investigating numerical anomalies or running deterministic-tolerance tests.
 
